invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_inverse.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: a step adds difference to xb wherever xa is odd, not only where the
  step swaps, so a subtraction that does not swap also moves xb to the old
  xa. The factors no longer describe the steps the approximations took,
  and the inverse is wrong. bin/p256_equiv_test holds both wide inverses to
  the 32-bit files' Fermat inverses, and p256_wide_inverse_steps holds a
  step to a reference that branches.

--- old
    *xb += difference & swap;
--- new
    *xb += difference & *odd;
